        "asr_text": "Every morning, I look for an empty desk. Someone may have used it yesterday, and someone else may use it tomorrow. I cannot keep papers in a drawer. I sometimes worry about using a desk or keyboard after someone else. I spend time finding a place before work starts. I miss having the same desk, drawer, and view. They helped me start without looking around and gave me a quiet feeling that I belonged there. Now the office can feel like a place I only borrow. I want my work and things to have a place, even when I cannot choose the desk rules.",
